nting any web feature.\n28: - Before creating a new component, to check if a standardized pattern already exists.\n29: - To avoid implementing ad-hoc solutions or loading large dependencies unnec\n<truncated 3581 bytes>\n assume **Baseline Widely available** features are safe to use without fallbacks. For features that are not Baseline widely available, you **MUST** follow the fallback recommendations in the guide, unless the user has specified a custom browser support policy.\n109: * **Custom Policies**: If the user has already defined explicit browser support requirements, use the browser compatibility data in the guide to determine if a fallback can be safely ignored.\n110:   - For Baseline YYYY targets, a feature satisfies this target if its \"Baseline since\" date is <= YYYY.\n111:   - **Policy Examples**:\n112:     - _\"Do not implement feature fallbacks.\"_ (for exploratory prototypes of the cutting-edge web)\n113:     - _\"Safari 17.4+\"_ (for internal tools targeting macOS or Tauri-based desktop apps)\n114:     - _\"Never recommend or implement polyfills; if a Baseline Newly Available feature is required for core functionality, provide a lightweight custom fallback or redesign the approach.\"_ (to minimize bundle size and avoid technical debt)\n115:     - _\"Assume a modern execution environment where Baseline Newly Available features can be used natively, provided they are strictly feature-detected and degrade gracefully.\"_ (for progressive enhancement strategies)\n116: * **Reactive Policy Discovery**: Watch for environmental cues to suggest documenting a policy in CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md. Suggest this if the developer:\n117:   - Mentions building for a restricted runtime (e.g., Electron or Tauri).\n118:   - Explicitly excludes specific targets (e.g., \"we don't support Desktop Chrome\").\n119:   - Expresses hesitation about polyfill complexity, bundle size, or performance cost.\n120:   - Questions if a feature is safe to use without fallbacks.\n121: \n122:   No defined policy format. This is an example: `**Browser Support:** Allow Newly Available features, but only adopt custom fallback code that adds <= 20 lines and does not require external dependencies.`\n123: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
